# spinofin panel logo. Two extensions can own the panel logo on Bluefin:
#   - custom-command-list (icon NAME -> themed symbolic lookup, recolored)
#   - Logo-menu (custom icon FILE PATH; St still recolors *-symbolic.svg, which
#     is how Bluefin's own ublue-logo-symbolic.svg renders through this path)
# We set both so whichever is active shows the spinofin mark as a fallback
# default. Deliberately UNLOCKED: a locked key can't be changed by the user at
# all -- not just here, but also from inside the extensions' own preference
# UIs, which write via plain gsettings.set_*() with no lock-awareness (neither
# extension checks Gio.Settings.is_writable() before writing), so a locked key
# makes their icon picker silently fail to persist a user's selection with no
# error shown. This system default is only a fallback for accounts with no
# explicit per-user value; see the autostart entry
# (etc/xdg/autostart/spinofin-branding-migrate-user-logo.desktop) for how
# spinofin still applies its own mark on fresh installs and on rebase from an
# existing Bluefin install without permanently overriding user choice. See
# custom/branding/README.md ("User-Customizable Panel Logo").
[org/gnome/shell/extensions/custom-command-list]
menuicon-setting='spinofin-logo-symbolic'

[org/gnome/shell/extensions/Logo-menu]
use-custom-icon=true
custom-icon-path='/usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/actions/spinofin-logo-symbolic.svg'
symbolic-icon=true
